; A `.cbor` payload whose TARGET is a bare fixed value (`bytes .cbor 42`), in MEMBER / element
; position. Generates under EVERY profile; the row is the regression carrier for that.
;
; Without encodings a fixed value stores nothing, so the `Fixed` deserialize branch evaluates to the
; unit `()` and emits it through whatever before/after wrapper its caller supplies — including the
; staging expression a `.cbor` overload wraps its target's read in. Where the wrapper binds nothing
; the line is suppressed instead, so a caller that supplies none (which is every caller outside a
; payload) gets the same bytes it always got.
;
; The class covers every fixed kind (`42`, `"s"`, `true`, `null`) and both the bare and the keyed
; element spellings — it keys on `Fixed` under a `.cbor` chain, not on the constant or the key.
; Two neighbours are deliberately NOT it:
;   - the rule-BODY spelling `x = bytes .cbor 42` is refused GRACEFULLY one seam earlier, by the
;     bare-fixed-value rule-body rejection, and never reaches the deserialize walk;
;   - a TAG between the `.cbor` and the constant (`bytes .cbor #6.1(42)`) still emits unparseable
;     Rust, because the value-less test matches a bare fixed root only — ledgered in
;     cddl-matrix/ROADMAP.md § findings, `A `.cbor` payload over a TAGGED fixed value` entry.
;
; This row is generate-only, so it holds the ABORT class alone. That the emitted crate builds and
; round-trips byte-exactly — payload verified, payload exhaustion enforced, non-minimal payload
; heads preserved — is pinned by
; `cbor_payload_over_fixed_value_generates_and_round_trips_on_every_profile`.
;
; Surfaced by the recombination sweep (`outer=arr_single inner=cbor_payload filler=type2.value`)
; once the tagged-optional member kind reshuffled its seeded draws onto the composition.
x = [bytes .cbor 42]
